# PeoplePay360 Cursor Rules

## Backend Architecture
- Strict 4-layer chain: `routes` → `controllers` → `services` → `repositories` → `db`.
- Routes `<module>.routes.ts` only map path + verb to controller. No validation or logic.
- Controllers `<module>.controller.ts` parse with Zod, invoke ONE service method, wrap with `asyncHandler`.
- Services `<module>.service.ts` contain all business logic. Pure functions, no `req`/`res`.
- Repositories `<module>.repository.ts` execute Drizzle queries using `@/shared/db`.
- Single central database in `src/shared/db.ts` and `src/db/schema.ts` (Neon Postgres).
- SCHEMA SYNC MANDATE: Any schema update MUST also update `DATABASE_SCHEMA.md`.

## Frontend Architecture
- Feature-driven modules in `src/features/<feature>/` with `components/`, `pages/`, `queries/`.
- Colocated queries: Request/response types, private fetcher, and exported React Query hook live together in `queries/`.
- No separate `types.ts` per feature. No `index.ts` barrel files. Direct imports are standard.
- Global network client in `@/api/apiClient` with 401 refresh queue.

## Strict Language Rules
- ALWAYS use `type` instead of `interface` across all TypeScript files.
- Strictly adhere to `DESIGN.md`: Editorial B&W, Playfair Display serif headlines, IBM Plex Sans body, single violet accent `#6A3FA0`, hairline borders, no shadows/gradients.
